Baret
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

# --- COLOR ---
# [] tea cup chipped at the rim, handle worn smooth from repeated grip
# [] Reshîd clan band visible at the wrist, the leather faded but the metal still bright
# [] thumb tracing the edge of the cup where the chipped rim meets the clay
# [] steam rising in a thin spiral from the cup, curling just above the rim
# [] linen collar of his tunic slightly frayed at the edge, tucked too tightly
# [] knee resting on the bedroll, the fabric of his trousers worn thin at the joint
# [] voice low and warm, the cadence shifting subtly when he says "nephew"
# [] fingers tapping a slow rhythm on the cup's side, not quite keeping time with his words
# [] tea leaves floating in the cup, not yet settled at the bottom
# [] shadow of the pylon stretching across the rock, long and sharp in the low sun
# [] small scar on the back of his right hand, healed white, shaped like a knife-cut
# [] laughter caught halfway, the sound cut off mid-breath when he realizes he's said it again
# --- end ---

FIXME(mundane): Baret is across from you at the rest circle, holding his teacup with both hands.

FIXME(mundane): You ask him how a Reshîd elder's son ends up on a Kesharat infrastructure crew. He has an explanation ready. It is fine for one question. When you follow up the explanation thins out. He fills the seam with another sentence about his nephew and moves past it without seeming to notice the seam was there.

choices:

* Step back to the circle = Let the conversation end
